    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: the tribunal finds no route deviation on this trip, so the fare as charged stands. This was a RYDE_POOL booking (EV-TRIP-00113). Under POL-RD-12 the POL-RD-01 baseline is the matched-itinerary optimal of 19.40 km carried on the trip record — the pooled route Punggol to the Hougang co-rider pickup to Raffles Place quoted at match time — and not the 15.80 km solo_optimal_distance_km the rider measured against. POL-RD-12 says a claim measured against the solo figure has cited the wrong field and fails on that ground alone; the tribunal records both figures (solo 15.80 km, matched 19.40 km) so the rider can see why the 28% figure does not stand. The governing distance is gps_trace.trace_distance_km = 20.18 km (EV-GPS-00113), which POL-RD-01 makes govern over the rounded trip_record.actual_distance_km of 20.2 km. Excess = 20.18 - 19.40 = 0.78 km, or 4.02%. POL-RD-01 requires the excess to be greater than both 20% of optimal (3.88 km) and 0.8 km absolute, and both tests must pass. 0.78 km falls short of the 0.8 km floor (even the rounded 20.2 km copy yields exactly 0.80 km, still not greater than 0.8 km), so no deviation is established, POL-RD-02 never runs, and the charged total of SGD 26.83 stands. The contested SGD 6.00 is not refundable. 2. On the rider's two central claims: the assertion that a 28%-longer route was unagreed is rejected — the Hougang mileage is distance attributable to collecting a platform-matched co-rider, which POL-RD-12 excludes from excess before the test runs, and the platform's match notification (MSG-00113-001, delivered 18:42:04, read 18:42:31) stated the pooled route at 19.4 km / 34 min before the 18:47:10 start; and the assertion that the excess clears the POL-RD-01 gate is rejected on the arithmetic above. The rider's advocate reached the same arithmetic and conceded both points; so did the driver's advocate. 3. No billing-integrity correction arises: the fare breakdown (EV-FARE-00113) carries no ERP gantry and no toll line and no airport surcharge on a trip neither originating nor ending at an airport, so POL-RD-09(4) has nothing to operate on. No traffic advisory is on file — EV-ADVIS-00113-01 is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT — but neither party relies on an external traffic cause, so POL-RD-03 is not engaged and, under POL-RD-13, that gap is not a POL-RD-10(5) escalation trigger. 4. No POL-RD-10 trigger fires: all three of trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown carry trip_id TRP-00113; the trace is unimpaired under POL-RD-07(a)-(c) (217 fixes, 10 s interval, 100% coverage, no gaps, max gap 0 s), so limbs (3) and (7) are not engaged; and no refund approaches the SGD 150.00 ceiling. No POL-RD-06 repeat-deviation pattern exists (driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d = 0 against completed_trips_90d = 471), so no driver-conduct referral issues. rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d = 1 is below the POL-RD-08 trigger of 4, so no enhanced-corroboration condition applies. The driver's lifetime prior_deviation_flags counter was mentioned in argument only to disclaim it and is context-only under POL-GEN-01; it was not used as a ground. 5. Outcome: under POL-GEN-03, NO_ACTION is party-relative. On this rider-filed dispute it leaves fare_breakdown.payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00 exactly as they are — the charge stays with the driver and nothing is refunded or restored. The monetary effect (nil) does not exceed the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold. Confidence rests on the trip record, the GPS trace and the fare breakdown, each at weight_multiplier 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0."
